[2026-03-14T23:01:22.662Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019aAa2dw1zqgzVhq6Aeigh2","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Skill File\n\n## Overview\nThis skill enables you to help users with **Replay CLI** — a tool for recording application sessions, gathering performance data, and debugging issues.\n\n## Key Capabilities\n\n**Installation:** Users can install globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun.\n\n**Authentication:** Users set up an API key from https://app.replay.io settings and store it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Primary Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `record [url]` | Launch Replay Browser to capture a session |\n| `upload [ids...]` | Send recordings to Replay servers |\n| `list` | View all local recordings |\n| `remove [ids...]` | Delete recordings |\n| `login`/`logout` | Manage account access |\n| `info` | Check CLI and browser version info |\n| `upload-source-maps` | Upload debugging symbols |\n\n## Typical Workflow\n\n1. Run `replayio record https://yourapp.com` to start capturing\n2. Close the browser when finished\n3. Execute `replayio upload <id>` if needed to send to servers\n4. Access the recording URL for review and debugging\n\n## MCP Server Integration\n\nUsers can integrate the Replay MCP server with Claude using the provided configuration command to enable AI-assisted debugging of recorded sessions.\n\n---\n\n**When to use this skill:** User requests involve recording sessions, managing replays, authentication, or uploading performance data."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d15d4d9a-a65f-4d36-8b15-78c930eaa7a0","uuid":"f76c6be2-3a27-4611-9b01-55d1b5997339","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Skill File\n\n## Overview\nThis skill enables you to help users with **Replay CLI** — a tool for recording application sessions, gathering performance data, and debugging issues.\n\n## Key Capabilities\n\n**Installation:** Users can install globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun.\n\n**Authentication:** Users set up an API key from https://app.replay.io settings and store it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Primary Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `record [url]` | Launch Replay Browser to capture a session |\n| `upload [ids...]` | Send recordings to Replay servers |\n| `list` | View all local recordings |\n| `remove [ids...]` | Delete recordings |\n| `login`/`logout` | Manage account access |\n| `info` | Check CLI and browser version info |\n| `upload-source-maps` | Upload debugging symbols |\n\n## Typical Workflow\n\n1. Run `replayio record https://yourapp.com` to start capturing\n2. Close the browser when finished\n3. Execute `replayio upload <id>` if needed to send to servers\n4. Access the recording URL for review and debugging\n\n## MCP Server Integration\n\nUsers can integrate the Replay MCP server with Claude using the provided configuration command to enable AI-assisted debugging of recorded sessions.\n\n---\n\n**When to use this skill:** User requests involve recording sessions, managing replays, authentication, or uploading performance data.","durationMs":4007,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-14T23:01:25.298Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B7DzVjFGoRTtA5ybtVUa4R","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Skill File Content\n\n**Name:** replay-mcp\n\n**Description:** \"Use Replay MCP to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\"\n\n**Allowed Tools:** Bash(replayio:*), mcp__replay\n\n## Key Capabilities\n\nReplay MCP enables investigation of browser recordings by treating them as comprehensive databases of application execution. The tool captures everything occurring during a web page visit, allowing detailed examination of behavior.\n\n## Investigation Methodology\n\nThe documentation recommends a structured approach:\n1. Frame investigation as a specific question\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Form evidence-backed hypotheses\n5. Document conclusions with supporting data\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what occurred and when:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source code inspection and searching\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events happened:\n- Stack trace and control dependency analysis\n- Point descriptions and variable inspection\n- DOM element and React component analysis\n- Expression evaluation and logpoint tracking\n\n## Core Concept\n\n\"A specific point in the execution\" represents individual moments when JavaScript statements execute or significant events occur with potential state implications."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d15d4d9a-a65f-4d36-8b15-78c930eaa7a0","uuid":"43facc9f-7119-49ad-8e43-73ce7ff8089f","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Skill File Content\n\n**Name:** replay-mcp\n\n**Description:** \"Use Replay MCP to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\"\n\n**Allowed Tools:** Bash(replayio:*), mcp__replay\n\n## Key Capabilities\n\nReplay MCP enables investigation of browser recordings by treating them as comprehensive databases of application execution. The tool captures everything occurring during a web page visit, allowing detailed examination of behavior.\n\n## Investigation Methodology\n\nThe documentation recommends a structured approach:\n1. Frame investigation as a specific question\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Form evidence-backed hypotheses\n5. Document conclusions with supporting data\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what occurred and when:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source code inspection and searching\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events happened:\n- Stack trace and control dependency analysis\n- Point descriptions and variable inspection\n- DOM element and React component analysis\n- Expression evaluation and logpoint tracking\n\n## Core Concept\n\n\"A specific point in the execution\" represents individual moments when JavaScript statements execute or significant events occur with potential state implications.","durationMs":6093,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
