[2026-03-14T23:01:29.447Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VQc5LAindk8FiUCK4X4Giv","type":"tool_result","content":"788:#### Test: Host Dashboard displays navigation tabs for Listings and Bookings\n789-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host.\n790-- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n791-- **Expected:** Below the stats overview, two tabs are visible: \"Listings\" and \"Bookings\". The \"Listings\" tab is active/selected by default.\n792-\n793-#### Test: Switching between Listings and Bookings tabs\n794-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host and on `/hosting` with the \"Listings\" tab active.\n795-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Bookings\" tab.\n796-- **Expected:** The Bookings tab content is displayed (table of bookings). The \"Bookings\" tab appears active/selected. User clicks \"Listings\" tab again and the listings grid is displayed.\n797-\n798-### Component: ListingsTab\n799-\n800-#### Test: Listings tab displays host's properties in a grid\n801-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with 3 active properties: \"Beach House\" ($150/night), \"Mountain Cabin\" ($200/night), \"City Loft\" ($120/night).\n802-- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting` (Listings tab is active by default).\n803-- **Expected:** A grid of 3 property cards is displayed. Each card shows the property title, main image, price per night, and status (active/inactive).\n804-\n805-#### Test: Listing card shows property details\n806-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with a property: title \"Beach House\", price $150/night, city \"Malibu\", 4.5 average rating, 10 reviews, active status.\n807-- **Expected:** The listing card displays the property title \"Beach House\", price \"$150/night\", location \"Malibu\", average rating \"4.5\" with star icon, review count \"10 reviews\", and a green \"Active\" badge.\n808-\n809-#### Test: Listing card has Edit button that navigates to property detail\n810-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with a property (id \"prop-123\").\n811-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Edit\" button on the property card.\n812-- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/properties/prop-123` where the host can view and edit their property details.\n813-\n814-#### Test: Listing card has Deactivate button for active properties\n815-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with an active property \"Beach House\".\n816-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Deactivate\" button on the \"Beach House\" card.\n817-- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears asking \"Are you sure you want to deactivate this listing?\". The dialog shows the property name \"Beach House\".\n818-\n819-#### Test: Confirming deactivation sets property to inactive\n820-- **Initial state:** The deactivation confirmation dialog is open for \"Beach House\".\n821-- **Action:** User clicks the confirm button (e.g., \"Yes, Deactivate\").\n822-- **Expected:** The app calls `DELETE /api/properties/:id` (which sets `is_active` to false). The dialog closes. The property card updates to show an \"Inactive\" status badge (gray or muted). A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Listing deactivated\"). The stats overview updates the \"Total Listings\" count to reflect the change.\n823-\n824-#### Test: Dismissing deactivation dialog keeps property active\n825-- **Initial state:** The deactivation confirmation dialog is open for \"Beach House\".\n826-- **Action:** User clicks the dismiss/cancel button.\n827-- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The property remains active with no changes.\n828-\n829-#### Test: Listing card shows Activate button for inactive properties\n830-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with an inactive property \"Old Cabin\".\n831-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Activate\" button on the \"Old Cabin\" card.\n832-- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/properties/:id` to set `is_active` to true. The property card updates to show a green \"Active\" badge. The \"Total Listings\" stat updates.\n833-\n834-#### Test: Listings tab shows empty state for host with no properties\n835-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with no properties.\n836-- **Expected:** The Listings tab displays an empty state message (e.g., \"You don't have any listings yet\") and a prominent \"Add Listing\" button or call-to-action.\n837-\n838-#### Test: Add Listing button is visible on the Listings tab\n839-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host.\n840-- **Expected:** An \"Add Listing\" button is prominently displayed on the Listings tab (e.g., in the header area or as a floating action button). The button has clear text \"Add Listing\" or a \"+\" icon with label.\n841-\n842-#### Test: Deactivate and activate actions work on repeated use\n843-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with two active properties.\n844-- **Action:** User deactivates the first property (confirms dialog), then activates it again, then deactivates the second property.\n845-- **Expected:** Each action updates the correct property's status. The stats overview correctly reflects the current count of active listings after each action.\n846-\n847-### Component: BookingsTab\n848-\n849-#### Test: Bookings tab displays table of bookings for host's properties\n850-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have bookings from various guests.\n851-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Bookings\" tab.\n852-- **Expected:** A table is displayed with columns: Property, Guest, Check-in, Check-out, Guests, Total, Status, and Actions. Each booking is a row in the table.\n853-\n854-#### Test: Bookings table shows correct data for each booking\n855-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. A booking exists: property \"Beach House\", guest \"Alice Smith\", check-in \"2026-07-01\", check-out \"2026-07-05\", 2 guests, total $750, status \"confirmed\".\n856-- **Expected:** The table row displays: \"Beach House\", \"Alice Smith\", \"Jul 1, 2026\", \"Jul 5, 2026\", \"2\", \"$750\", a green \"Confirmed\" status badge.\n857-\n858-#### Test: Bookings tab has status filter controls\n859-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab.\n860-- **Expected:** Filter controls are visible above the table allowing the host to filter by status: \"All\", \"Pending\", \"Confirmed\", \"Cancelled\", \"Completed\". \"All\" is selected by default.\n861-\n862-#### Test: Filtering bookings by Pending status\n863-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. Bookings exist with statuses \"pending\", \"confirmed\", and \"completed\".\n864-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Pending\" status filter.\n865-- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"pending\" are displayed in the table. The \"Pending\" filter appears active/selected.\n866-\n867-#### Test: Filtering bookings by Confirmed status\n868-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab with various bookings."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d15d4d9a-a65f-4d36-8b15-78c930eaa7a0","uuid":"c1456aee-32c3-450a-888e-e37fa45b0074","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"788:#### Test: Host Dashboard displays navigation tabs for Listings and Bookings\n789-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host.\n790-- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n791-- **Expected:** Below the stats overview, two tabs are visible: \"Listings\" and \"Bookings\". The \"Listings\" tab is active/selected by default.\n792-\n793-#### Test: Switching between Listings and Bookings tabs\n794-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host and on `/hosting` with the \"Listings\" tab active.\n795-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Bookings\" tab.\n796-- **Expected:** The Bookings tab content is displayed (table of bookings). The \"Bookings\" tab appears active/selected. User clicks \"Listings\" tab again and the listings grid is displayed.\n797-\n798-### Component: ListingsTab\n799-\n800-#### Test: Li